    "Sorting every distinct value by its count works. Is there a way to avoid fully sorting when you only need k of them, for example a heap?",
    "A count can never be larger than the length of nums. How could you use that to index values by their count and read off the biggest ones directly?",
    "Count with a dict, drop each value into a bucket indexed by its frequency (a list of length n + 1), then walk the buckets from the highest frequency down, collecting values until you have k."
